From 98fb68e3c0cd3b023c7651660d9215083b40d004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max <maxobremer@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:43:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Card Style setting with a Vanilla+ card, and the wide
 save button on Classic cards

Adds a world setting, Card Style, for dnd5e 6 cards:

- Classic RSReforged (default): unchanged, plus the 4.x full-width saving
  throw button under the roll sections. The button forwards its click to
  dnd5e's own rollSave button.
- Vanilla+: dnd5e's own compact roll rows are moved from each native child
  message onto the usage card (native-vanilla.js). RSReforged draws no roll
  there; it adds Disadvantage / Advantage / Critical Hit / Bonus buttons to
  each breakdown, stamps the breakdown's dice so click-to-reroll and GM
  fudging work, and applies Hide NPC Roll Results and the Always Roll
  Multiple Dice extra d20.

The retroactive advantage and critical edits are extracted from the classic
overlay closures in native-card.js (retroAdvantage, retroCritical) so both
styles run the same code, and damageDieSources exposes the die-to-roll
mapping the classic damage breakdown already used. No change to the
workflow, the messages, or the classic rendering.

Tests: 23 new (native-vanilla, native-card-style, native-card); suite 440 passing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wKoNNHQkHRMGJVpmsBo1W
